 "caveats": [
  "SURVIVOR BIAS: survivors-only backtest universe, so CAGR is an UPPER BOUND. Of ~721 S&P names that left the index 2011-2026, only ~40 are genuine bankruptcies (the rest are M&A / ticker-changes, NOT losses) and are excluded from the panel. The failure-bias is bounded (momentum/quality screens avoid most pre-bankruptcy names) but real - not a survivorship-free track record.",
  "TRUE daily mark-to-market metrics \u2014 the -37% drawdown is the real intra-period low (COVID 2020), not the smoothed rebalance-spaced figure.",
  "Top-3 concentration: high single-name risk. Held 70 distinct names over the backtest, rotating ~3 at a time.",
  "Frictionless backtest: ignores ~226%/yr turnover cost, slippage, and short-term-gains tax. Net returns will be lower.",
  "Valuation pillar de-contaminated with authoritative yfinance splits (2026-06-17). EDGAR-era 2011-2026, point-in-time S&P membership.",
  "Backtest through 2026-05-07 (panel data limit). OOS column = untouched 2021-2026 holdout."
 ]
